  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/env-wt/603",
  "definition": "Water Depth Supporting Information Required",
  "effectiveDate": "2019-12-15",
  "historyNote": "#12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-Wt 603.08",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 603.08 Water Depth Supporting Information Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 603.08 Water Depth Supporting Information Required.\n\n(a) Using current predicted NOAA tidal datum for the location, and tying field measurements to NAVD 88, field observations of at least 3 tide events, including at least one minus tide event, shall be located to document the range of the tide in the proposed location showing the following levels:\n\n(1) Mean lower low water;\n\n(2) Mean low water;\n\n(3) Mean high water;\n\n(4) Mean tide level;\n\n(5) Mean higher high water;\n\n(6) Highest observable tide line; and\n\n(7) Predicted sea-level rise as identified in the vulnerability assessment in Env-Wt 603.05.\n\n(b) The following data shall be presented in the application project narrative to support how water depths were determined:\n\n(1) The date, time of day, and weather conditions when water depths were recorded; and\n\n(2) The name and license number of the licensed land surveyor who conducted the field measurements.\n\n(c) For tidal stream crossing projects, provide water depth information to show how the tier 4 stream crossing is designed to meet Env-Wt 904.07(c) and (d), and for repair, rehabilitation, or replacement of tier 4 stream crossings, demonstrate how the requirements of Env-Wt 904.09 are met.\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
}
